\section*{Abstract}
\begin{itemize}
\item Completed: passage preparation, BM25, flat BGE retrieval, and baseline evaluation.
\item MultiHop-RAG: 609 articles, 6,638 passages, 2,556 questions.
\item Recall@50: BM25 0.9092; dense 0.9286.
\item HHSI and HotpotQA experiments remain planned.
\end{itemize}

\section*{1. Introduction: research questions}
\begin{itemize}
\item Does combining semantic similarity and entity overlap improve evidence coverage?
\item Does multi-branch retrieval recover more supporting articles than flat retrieval?
\item What are the retrieval gains and indexing/search costs?
\end{itemize}


\section*{2. Related work}
\begin{itemize}
\item Review BM25 and Dense Passage Retrieval for flat retrieval background.
\item Review HotpotQA and MultiHop-RAG for multi-hop evidence retrieval.
\item Compare RAPTOR, SiReRAG, HiRAG, and HippoRAG with proposed HHSI.
\item RAPTOR comparison: discuss hierarchy construction, summaries, and entity signals.
\item Verify paper details before claiming missing entity awareness or hierarchy.
\item Present HHSI benefits as hypotheses; no HHSI results exist yet.
\end{itemize}

\section*{3. Methodology}
\subsection*{Passage construction --- completed}
\begin{itemize}
\item Chunk article bodies; retain titles and source metadata separately.
\item Maximum 256 BGE tokens, including special tokens.
\item Whole-sentence overlap up to 32 tokens; split long sentences when needed.
\item Use spaCy blank English with a rule-based sentencizer.
\item Keep passage IDs, document IDs, and URLs for source mapping.
\item Validated all 609 articles; no coverage failures.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Semantic and entity representations}
\begin{itemize}
\item Completed: BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5; 768-dimensional embeddings.
\item CLS pooling, L2 normalization, exact cosine search; query instruction prefix.
\item Entity extraction is pending; current spaCy pipeline performs segmentation only.
\item Specify NER model, retained entity types, and string normalization after implementation.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Hierarchy and retrieval --- proposed}
\begin{itemize}
\item Draft design: cosine similarity plus entity Jaccard overlap.
\item Draft hierarchy: average-linkage clustering, centroid vectors, aggregated entity sets.
\item Still define subsets, stopping rules, depth, and empty-entity handling.
\item Draft search: retain multiple branches, reach passages, then rerank.
\item Still define beam width and final reranking score.
\item Alpha controls index similarity; lambda controls query-to-node scoring.
\item Neither weight has been selected or tested.
\item Proposed tuning: compare several weights on held-out development questions.
\item Include semantic-only and entity-only settings; freeze choices before final testing.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Evaluation: datasets}
\begin{itemize}
\item Completed dataset: MultiHop-RAG news articles and multi-hop questions.
\item Evaluate 2,255 questions with evidence; exclude 301 null queries from metrics.
\item Null queries remain in retrieval outputs with null evaluation scores.
\item HotpotQA Wikipedia experiments are pending; specify setup and split later.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Evaluation: metrics and comparisons}
\begin{itemize}
\item Cutoffs: top 5, 10, 20, and 50 passages.
\item Recall@k: fraction of gold article URLs recovered.
\item MRR@k: reciprocal rank of the first relevant passage; zero if absent.
\item All-Hop Coverage@k: whether every gold article URL is recovered.
\item Average across evaluated questions; duplicate articles still occupy passage ranks.
\item URL matching measures article coverage, not exact supporting-fact retrieval.
\item Completed comparisons: BM25 and flat BGE on the same passages and questions.
\item Pending: RAPTOR, HHSI, and downstream QA with EM and token F1.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Design limitations}
\begin{itemize}
\item Jaccard gives interpretable entity overlap; missed entities and aliases can hurt it.
\item Dense similarity may complement missing entity overlap; test this claim.
\item Measure clustering time and memory before claiming scalability.
\end{itemize}

\section*{4. Experimental results}
\begin{itemize}
\item Add a MultiHop-RAG table using the following saved results.
\item Values below: Recall@k / MRR@k / All-Hop Coverage@k.
\item BM25: k=5: 0.5787 / 0.7447 / 0.2829; k=10: 0.7049 / 0.7544 / 0.4262.
\item BM25: k=20: 0.8167 / 0.7563 / 0.5911; k=50: 0.9092 / 0.7566 / 0.7698.
\item Dense: k=5: 0.5329 / 0.7077 / 0.2302; k=10: 0.6772 / 0.7185 / 0.3814.
\item Dense: k=20: 0.8001 / 0.7204 / 0.5539; k=50: 0.9286 / 0.7208 / 0.8182.
\item BM25 leads at smaller cutoffs; dense leads Recall and All-Hop Coverage at 50.
\item Label MRR@50 explicitly; unrestricted MRR was not measured.
\item Mark HHSI, RAPTOR, HotpotQA, and QA scores as pending.
\end{itemize}

\section*{5. Planned analysis}
\begin{itemize}
\item Implement NER, hybrid hierarchy, and multi-branch search.
\item Test alpha, lambda, beam width, and hierarchy settings.
\item Compare semantic-only, entity-only, and hybrid variants.
\item Add RAPTOR, HotpotQA, and downstream QA experiments.
\item Inspect missed evidence; compare build time, memory, and comparable query latency.
\end{itemize}

